  <section id="why-the-answers-drift">
    <h2><span class="num">1.4</span>Why the answers drift</h2>
    <p>
      One fund has to follow several sets of rules at once: Luxembourg law, EU law, tax rules, and the
      rules of each country where it is sold. Each set has its own regulator, deadlines and wording, so
      the same report can be described differently in different places. The project’s test data covers
      several of these layers.
    </p>
